Circle in xAce-baremetal
========================

This folder is a copy of the Circle C++ bare metal environment for the
Raspberry Pi, by Rene Stange, used to build xAce-baremetal:

    Project:  https://github.com/rsta2/circle
    Version:  Step51.1.1
    Commit:   7a81e1b480fe7d19fc1fc695b89bff0a0848f44b
              (25 September 2026, "Merge branch 'hotfix-51.1.1'")

It was a git submodule of xAce-baremetal; it is now a plain copy, so that
the project builds from its own sources alone.

The files are those of that commit, unchanged, except:

  * Circle's own submodule addon/lvgl/lvgl (LVGL graphics library) is not
    included: its folder is empty. xAce-baremetal does not use it.

  * Circle's own submodule addon/wlan/hostap (the WPA supplicant, for Wi-Fi)
    is included in part: https://github.com/rsta2/hostap at the commit
    Step51.1.1 uses, 966cab4a3bc958e7ff304a46d91a6172a1bfecaf, with only the
    files Circle's wpa_supplicant/Makefile.circle builds from (sources and
    headers), plus COPYING, README and CONTRIBUTIONS. One file is changed:
    wpa_supplicant/main_circle.cpp has two functions added for xAce-baremetal,
    wpa_supplicant_is_running() and wpa_supplicant_reload() (marked "Added for
    xAce-baremetal"). hostap is licensed under the BSD license, see
    addon/wlan/hostap/COPYING.

  * lib/net/httpdaemon.cpp: CHTTPDaemon::ParseRequest() checks that the path
    of the request URI (before any "?") fits m_RequestPath (HTTP_MAX_PATH);
    a longer one overran it. Marked "xAce-baremetal".

  * Config.mk (Circle's build configuration, ignored by Circle's .gitignore)
    is copied in by ../build.sh from ../circle-config/Config.mk: Raspberry Pi
    model, 32-bit mode and the project's toolchain.

Build output (*.o, *.a, *.d, ...) is ignored by Circle's .gitignore.

Circle is licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3, see
LICENSE in this folder.

To update Circle, replace this folder with the files of a newer commit of
https://github.com/rsta2/circle (keeping this file and updating it), then
rebuild everything: ./build.sh cleans and rebuilds when the model changes;
otherwise run "./makeall clean" here first.
